  "message": "Yes — I know what you mean. A Hub 75 is the standard LED matrix panel interface (the 16‑ or 32‑pin connector pattern you see on many RGB LED displays), commonly used for modular LED panels in signs and video walls. People call them Hub75 panels, and there are different manufacturers and pinout variants (those Lehman/Karun names sound like vendor or model families you’re mapping).  \n\nIf you want, I can open a browser search for Hub75 datasheets or show the team what analysts we have who might map vendor parts — which would you prefer?",
